(3154861, 442629, 30049, '<td valign="top">Somebody has TOO much time on their hands.  :D  Cute!  I think I would have lost the white thing in the back right, it''s distracting and unidentifiable (at least to me).  A white backdrop would have been stronger - or - if you wanted to continue the festive mood, try something like crinkled tinfoil or something?  Just a thought.  Best of luck to you in the challenge.</td>', 'Somebody has TOO much time on their hands.  :D  Cute!  I think I would have lost the white thing in the back right, it''s distracting and unidentifiable (at least to me).  A white backdrop would have been stronger - or - if you wanted to continue the festive mood, try something like crinkled tinfoil or something?  Just a thought.  Best of luck to you in the challenge.', '2006-12-27 23:06:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(3154868, 442713, 30049, '<td valign="top">How can you tell who''s who?  King, Queen, etc...  :D  The subject seems too distant.  Did you try cropping this down (or capturing initially) where you zoomed in on the board more, even losing some of the board and maybe a piece or two?  I don''t know, just a thought.  Something seems out of balance.  JMO of course.  Good luck in the challenge.</td>', 'How can you tell who''s who?  King, Queen, etc...  :D  The subject seems too distant.  Did you try cropping this down (or capturing initially) where you zoomed in on the board more, even losing some of the board and maybe a piece or two?  I don''t know, just a thought.  Something seems out of balance.  JMO of course.  Good luck in the challenge.', '2006-12-27 23:09:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(3154873, 442415, 30049, '<td valign="top">He''s back!  This dude gets around.  :D  I like the concept, it''s clever.  The image itself is underexposed substantially.  Use your custom white balance to get your whites white, curves and levels are also tools to help get your whites &amp; blacks in line.  Good luck in the challenge.</td>', 'He''s back!  This dude gets around.  :D  I like the concept, it''s clever.  The image itself is underexposed substantially.  Use your custom white balance to get your whites white, curves and levels are also tools to help get your whites & blacks in line.  Good luck in the challenge.', '2006-12-27 23:11:48.000000', NULL, 1),
