(3174761, 442496, 69838, '<td valign="top">Thanks guys and gals for all the comments.  I''ve learned allot from this event.  Looking back I realize now that my ISO (400) was way too high.  It was on a tripod with a timer.  Obviously, my main issues were focus and graininess.  I will try to do better next time.  BTW, the camera is my new Kodak Easyshare z612.  I don''t believe it is at fault here.  But who knows.  Also, another thing that I have come to realize is that different monitors can make the image look much different.  I have an old CRT with lots of deep black levels.  The picture seems to look pretty good there.  I also have an LCD at work with reveals a few more blemishes.  Another friend of mine has an old IMac.  I''m not completely sure why, but the picture looks terrible on his monitor.  Anyway, I still have allot to learn.<br/> <br/>Thanks again for all your critiques.  :-)</td>', 'Thanks guys and gals for all the comments.  I''ve learned allot from this event.  Looking back I realize now that my ISO (400) was way too high.  It was on a tripod with a timer.  Obviously, my main issues were focus and graininess.  I will try to do better next time.  BTW, the camera is my new Kodak Easyshare z612.  I don''t believe it is at fault here.  But who knows.  Also, another thing that I have come to realize is that different monitors can make the image look much different.  I have an old CRT with lots of deep black levels.  The picture seems to look pretty good there.  I also have an LCD at work with reveals a few more blemishes.  Another friend of mine has an old IMac.  I''m not completely sure why, but the picture looks terrible on his monitor.  Anyway, I still have allot to learn. Thanks again for all your critiques.  :-)', '2007-01-03 09:54:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(3174845, 443011, 24454, '<td valign="top">Way to go Robin!!!!   Once again you have boldly made the ordinary extraordinary  :)   This was one of my favorites!  So glad it finished so strong!<br/> <br/></td>', 'Way to go Robin!!!!   Once again you have boldly made the ordinary extraordinary  :)   This was one of my favorites!  So glad it finished so strong! ', '2007-01-03 10:12:59.000000', NULL, 0),
