(3185614, 442422, 66952, '<td valign="top">Hey, I saw this in the underrated thread. I didn''t vote in this challenge, but I like the shot, and you seem interested in real comments, so I thought I''d chime in....I would have given it 6. The message is good, it''s nice and sharp (maybe a bit too sharp), and it''s original. I like the simple composition, probably because I tend to do the same kind of thing. I think there''s a couple of reasons it didn''t do better. For better or worse, in DPC, it only takes a couple of minor technical issues to drop the score a couple of points. The focus issue that Puckzzz mentioned, the out of level trash can, and the oversharpening probably took a full point off of your average. The other thing is that the lighting is a bit harsh. I think the other thing that might have hurt you is that people had to read the title to understand what the picture is about. I don''t know how you would do this theme another way, but a lot of people only look at the picture for a couple of seconds. If they have to do any reading, your score will drop.</td>', 'Hey, I saw this in the underrated thread. I didn''t vote in this challenge, but I like the shot, and you seem interested in real comments, so I thought I''d chime in....I would have given it 6. The message is good, it''s nice and sharp (maybe a bit too sharp), and it''s original. I like the simple composition, probably because I tend to do the same kind of thing. I think there''s a couple of reasons it didn''t do better. For better or worse, in DPC, it only takes a couple of minor technical issues to drop the score a couple of points. The focus issue that Puckzzz mentioned, the out of level trash can, and the oversharpening probably took a full point off of your average. The other thing is that the lighting is a bit harsh. I think the other thing that might have hurt you is that people had to read the title to understand what the picture is about. I don''t know how you would do this theme another way, but a lot of people only look at the picture for a couple of seconds. If they have to do any reading, your score will drop.', '2007-01-05 17:01:01.000000', NULL, 0),
