(3190567, 442899, 31905, '<td valign="top">Congrats.<br/>I must tell you though... your image featured in one of the leading news papers here in Bombay promoting DPCHALLENGE as a website for learning and entering contests. They had your image and a small write up on DPC. <br/>Even though I dont know whether they can use your image like that... it was heartening to see a familiar snap since I have been around for almost 2 years and this is first time I have seen DPC in mainstream media in India.<br/> <br/>Impressive stuff.</td>', 'Congrats.I must tell you though... your image featured in one of the leading news papers here in Bombay promoting DPCHALLENGE as a website for learning and entering contests. They had your image and a small write up on DPC. Even though I dont know whether they can use your image like that... it was heartening to see a familiar snap since I have been around for almost 2 years and this is first time I have seen DPC in mainstream media in India. Impressive stuff.', '2007-01-07 05:36:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(3191305, 441784, 29177, '<td valign="top">LOL! Oh geez... I missed this in the voting! I admire you pushing the envelope... sure did stir up lots of controversy :oP I have no problems with it.... well done.</td>', 'LOL! Oh geez... I missed this in the voting! I admire you pushing the envelope... sure did stir up lots of controversy :oP I have no problems with it.... well done.', '2007-01-07 12:41:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(3191659, 441784, 5885, '<td valign="top">I''m just back to compliment you on receiving such a wide variety of comments and votes...<br/> <br/>Art is about reaction and from the voting histogram you got reactions from all ends of the spectrum. <br/> <br/>You got hammered pretty hard on the low-end, but only one person would comment on technical merit (which I disagree with). <br/> <br/>Well done. :-) <br/> <br/>Now, I do wonder what the photo would have looked like if you had raised the dildo off the glass and kept only a reflection of it in the glass slightly out of focus. Compositionally, I think it would have been stronger, but at the same time would lose some of the in your face punch.<br/> <br/>As far as the "wash it" comments, I''m assuming that that translucent dildo has sparkles in it. I''m not sure how to make that more apparent without blowing highlights everywhere.</td>', 'I''m just back to compliment you on receiving such a wide variety of comments and votes... Art is about reaction and from the voting histogram you got reactions from all ends of the spectrum.  You got hammered pretty hard on the low-end, but only one person would comment on technical merit (which I disagree with).  Well done. :-)  Now, I do wonder what the photo would have looked like if you had raised the dildo off the glass and kept only a reflection of it in the glass slightly out of focus. Compositionally, I think it would have been stronger, but at the same time would lose some of the in your face punch. As far as the "wash it" comments, I''m assuming that that translucent dildo has sparkles in it. I''m not sure how to make that more apparent without blowing highlights everywhere.', '2007-01-07 14:55:31.000000', NULL, 0),
